se), which should not surprise us.\par }{\b\f210 6.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 P}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 rta}{\f208  designates the entrance (gate) of a city, }{\b\f210 j}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 nua}{\f208  that of a house. }{\b\f210 P}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 rt\u225\'87}{\f208  and }{\b\f210 v}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 \u225\'87}{\f208 , with a long }{\b\f210 \u225\'87}{\f208 , indicate, without the need for a preposition, the place}{\b\i\f212  through which one passes}{\f208 . With the other words one employs the preposition }{\b\f210 per}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 by, through}{\f208 ; }{\b\f210 per }{\f208 u}{\b\f210 rbem}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 across the city}{\f208 ; and (P 8), }{\b\f210 per v}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 cum}{\f208 .\par }{\b\f210 7.}{\f208  A}{\b\f210 quae S}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 xtiae}{\f208  (word-by-word, }{\i\f211 the waters of }{\b\f210 S}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 xtius}{\f208 ), }{\i\f211 Aix-en-Provence}{\f208 . Equally A}{\b\f210 quae Grati}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 nae}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 the waters of Gratian}{\f208  (emperor who gave his name to }{\b\f210 Gatian}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 polis}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 Grenoble}{\f208 ) became }{\i\f211 Aix-les-Bains}{\f208  (Savoy) and A}{\b\f210 quae Gr}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 ni}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 Aix-la-Chapelle}{\f208  (}{\i\f211 Aachen}{\f208 ).\par These }{\b\f210 Aquae}{\f208  (singular a}{\b\f210 qua}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 water}{\f208 ) were Roman thermal cities (cities built over hot springs), the second word serving to differentiate them from each other. Oddly enough in general it is the first word which has remained (Aix, Ax, Dax, Aachen).\par }{\b\f210 8.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 V}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 cus}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 the village}{\f208 , also indicates the street bordered by houses our of which villages grew.\par }{\b\f210 9.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 Sinistr}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 rsum}{\f208  (}{\i\f211 going}{\f208 ) }{\i\f211 towards the left}{\f208 ; }{\b\f210 sin}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 stra}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 the left hand}{\f208 ; }{\b\f210 sin}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 ster}{\f20